    "custom_liquid_NbFWLD": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "name": "FAQ Farsighted Mask",
      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "<section id=\"collection-faq-section\" class=\"faq-container\" aria-labelledby=\"collection-faq-title\">\n<h2 id=\"collection-faq-title\" class=\"faq-title\">Farsighted Snorkel Mask FAQ</h2>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">What is a farsighted snorkel mask?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>A farsighted prescription dive mask is designed for divers who need plus-power vision correction underwater. Instead of standard flat glass, these masks use optical corrective lenses that help bring nearby objects back into focus. They are especially useful for reading a gauge reader, checking equipment settings, or seeing details more clearly while snorkeling or scuba diving.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">How do plus lenses work underwater?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Plus lenses help compensate for hyperopia and presbyopia by adjusting how light enters the eye underwater. A hyperopia dive mask works by correcting how light reaches the eye, since water naturally changes visual perception and can magnify objects slightly. The right lens strength improves overall underwater focus without making vision feel overly strong or unnatural.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">Can I use a farsighted prescription mask for snorkeling and scuba diving?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Yes. Farsighted prescription masks are suitable for both snorkeling and prescription scuba diving. Whether you stay near the surface or dive deeper underwater, dive mask magnifying lenses and a secure silicone seal help maintain clear vision and reliable performance in the sea.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">Do I need the same diopter strength underwater as I use in glasses?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Usually not. Because water can magnify nearby objects, many farsighted divers feel more comfortable with slightly reduced positive diopter strength compared to their everyday glasses prescription. This differs from nearsighted prescriptions, which typically use negative lens correction underwater. This creates a more natural viewing experience underwater, especially when looking at objects both close and farther away.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">Can I choose different lens strengths for each eye?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Yes. Most Rx masks allow you to select a separate lens correction for each eye. This is helpful if your prescription differs between eyes or if one eye requires stronger optical correction than the other.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">Are farsighted Rx masks good for reading dive gauges underwater?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Absolutely. One of the biggest advantages of farsighted corrective lenses is improved close to medium-range clarity. Many divers use plus-lens masks specifically to improve their all round vision underwater, helping you see coral reefs and marine life clearer. In some cases they can be helpful to read dive computers, pressure gauges, camera settings, and other equipment more comfortably underwater.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">What makes a comfortable farsighted prescription dive mask fit?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>A comfortable fit depends on your face shape, mask size, and skirt design. Many divers prefer low volume masks with soft silicone and a twin-seal design because they reduce leaks and help divers stay comfortable and relaxed with natural breathing during longer dives or snorkeling sessions.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">Are bifocal lenses available for farsighted dive masks?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Some fully custom prescription dive masks may offer bifocal or reading-focused lens options. However, our farsighted prescription masks do not include bifocal lenses. Our lenses are single-vision, meaning the full lens is made in one strength to help improve overall distance vision underwater.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n</section>\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n\"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n\"mainEntity\": [\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"What is a farsighted snorkel mask?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"A farsighted prescription dive mask is designed for divers who need plus-power vision correction underwater. Instead of standard flat glass, these masks use optical corrective lenses that help bring nearby objects back into focus. They are especially useful for reading a gauge reader, checking equipment settings, or seeing details more clearly while snorkeling or scuba diving.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"How do plus lenses work underwater?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Plus lenses help compensate for hyperopia and presbyopia by adjusting how light enters the eye underwater. A hyperopia dive mask works by correcting how light reaches the eye, since water naturally changes visual perception and can magnify objects slightly. The right lens strength improves overall underwater focus without making vision feel overly strong or unnatural.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"Can I use a farsighted prescription mask for snorkeling and scuba diving?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Yes. Farsighted prescription masks are suitable for both snorkeling and prescription scuba diving. Whether you stay near the surface or dive deeper underwater, dive mask magnifying lenses and a secure silicone seal help maintain clear vision and reliable performance in the sea.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"Do I need the same diopter strength underwater as I use in glasses?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Usually not. Because water can magnify nearby objects, many farsighted divers feel more comfortable with slightly reduced positive diopter strength compared to their everyday glasses prescription. This differs from nearsighted prescriptions, which typically use negative lens correction underwater. This creates a more natural viewing experience underwater, especially when looking at objects both close and farther away.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"Can I choose different lens strengths for each eye?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Yes. Most Rx masks allow you to select a separate lens correction for each eye. This is helpful if your prescription differs between eyes or if one eye requires stronger optical correction than the other.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"Are farsighted Rx masks good for reading dive gauges underwater?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Absolutely. One of the biggest advantages of farsighted corrective lenses is improved close to medium-range clarity. Many divers use plus-lens masks specifically to improve their all round vision underwater, helping you see coral reefs and marine life clearer. In some cases they can be helpful to read dive computers, pressure gauges, camera settings, and other equipment more comfortably underwater.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"What makes a comfortable farsighted prescription dive mask fit?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"A comfortable fit depends on your face shape, mask size, and skirt design. Many divers prefer low volume masks with soft silicone and a twin-seal design because they reduce leaks and help divers stay comfortable and relaxed with natural breathing during longer dives or snorkeling sessions.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"Are bifocal lenses available for farsighted dive masks?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Some fully custom prescription dive masks may offer bifocal or reading-focused lens options. However, our farsighted prescription masks do not include bifocal lenses. Our lenses are single-vision, meaning the full lens is made in one strength to help improve overall distance vision underwater.\"\n}\n}\n]\n}\n</script>\n\n<style>\n.faq-container {\nmax-width: 700px;\nmargin: 20px auto;\npadding: 20px;\nborder-top: 1px solid #023059;\nfont-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;\n}\n.faq-title {\nfont-size: 24px;\nfont-weight: bold;\ncolor: #023059;\ntext-align: center;\nmargin-bottom: 15px;\n}\n.faq-item {\nborder-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\nmargin-bottom: 10px;\n}\n.faq-question {\nfont-size: 16px;\nbackground-color: #ffffff;\ncolor: #023059;\npadding: 10px;\ncursor: pointer;\nborder: 1px solid #023059;\nborder-radius: 5px;\nmargin: 0;\nfont-weight: 700;\ndisplay: flex;\nalign-items: baseline;\n}\n.faq-question h3 {\nfont-size: 16px;\ncolor: #023059;\nfont-weight: 700;\nmargin: 0;\n}\n.faq-answer {\npadding: 10px;\nfont-size: 14px;\nbackground-color: #f9f9f9;\ncolor: #023059;\nfont-weight: 500;\n}\n.faq-answer p { margin: 0 0 8px 0; }\n.faq-answer p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }\n.faq-answer a { color: #B95e05; text-decoration: none; }\n.faq-answer a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\ndetails summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }\ndetails[open] .faq-question::before { content: \"▾ \"; }\ndetails:not([open]) .faq-question::before { content: \"▸ \"; }\n</style>",
